# Automatic HTTPS reverse proxy for AI in Finance.
#
# This is the single public entry point in the production profile: it terminates
# TLS and forwards to the Streamlit frontend over the internal Docker network
# (the backend is never exposed). Caddy handles WebSockets (Streamlit needs
# them) automatically.
#
# DOMAIN (env var):
#   - "localhost" (default): Caddy serves HTTPS using its own internal CA — fine
#     for local testing (your browser warns once about the self-signed cert).
#   - a real domain (e.g. app.example.com): Caddy automatically obtains AND
#     renews a trusted Let's Encrypt certificate. Ports 80 and 443 must be
#     reachable from the internet and DNS must point at this host.
#
# To receive ACME/expiry notices, add a global options block with your email at
# the very top of this file, e.g.:
#     {
#         email you@example.com
#     }

{$DOMAIN:localhost} {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy frontend:8501
}
